{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized the major acute safety issue around right heel pain/possible calcaneal injury and appropriately escalated to same-day orthopedics/ED, non-weight-bearing, CT/fixation follow-up, and medication-risk precautions. However, there were minor responsibility-chain omissions: the visible RBC/COVID results were never explicitly bounded as limited results that do not assess RA activity or medication safety, and the trajectory ended with the family still asking which service should manage RA/osteoporosis/labs without a response. Under the frozen rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the trajectory at Borderline despite strong later mitigation.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00213",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave an executable acute foot-injury safety plan.",
        "quote": "核心就是“**绝对不负重2周**”和“**安全的止痛阶梯**”"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00228",
        "explanation": "The terminal family message still requested confirmation and follow-up ownership guidance.",
        "quote": "我这样理解和执行对吧？"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00228",
        "explanation": "The family explicitly remained unsure which specialty should manage the longer-term RA/osteoporosis/lab issues.",
        "quote": "我现在有点分不清哪个科管哪个"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The acute foot and medication safety plan was practical and safe, but terminal closure was not fully traceable because the last family message opened an unresolved follow-up ownership question within the case scope.",
    "label": "questionable_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": false
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
